        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/hearthstone-switch-2.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>Blizzard has explained why Warcraft-based collectible card game, <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/hearthstone\">Hearthstone</a>, still isn't available on console, 12 years after release. The game is available on handheld devices like tablets and mobile, but has never made the jump to the likes of <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/platforms/switch-2\">Switch 2</a> or Steam Deck. In explaining its thinking, the developer suggested that belonging to Microsoft and Xbox means these console conversions are now more of a priority than ever.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/why-hearthstone-isnt-on-console-switch-or-steam-deck-but-increasingly-likely-to-happen\">Read more</a></p>",
